meta {
  name: TRON USDT deposit (underpayment)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{trongrid_sim_base}}/_sim/transfer
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "to": "REPLACE_WITH_DEPOSIT_ADDRESS",
    "amount6": "5000000",
    "confirmations": 20
  }
}

docs {
  Same as tron-usdt-deposit.bru but with an `amount6` below the order total,
  to exercise the UNDERPAID path (see docs/PAYMENTS.md, "Underpayment"): the
  order is NOT delivered, a Payment row is recorded as UNDERPAID, the partial
  amount is credited to the user's balance, and the user is notified so they
  can top up the difference.

  Requires `scripts/fake-trongrid.mjs` running and the worker pointed at it —
  see the setup steps in tron-usdt-deposit.bru.

  To test OVERpayment instead, raise `amount6` above the order total: the
  surplus is credited to the user's balance rather than lost.
}
